const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文以概率模型连接财务比率、企业规模等会计信息与困境结果。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper links financial ratios, firm size, and other accounting information to distress outcomes through a probabilistic model. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源将多个报告变量放进概率预测框架，并围绕明确的困境标签和样本定义讨论结果。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It places multiple reported variables in a probability-prediction framework with an explicit distress label and sample definition. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"必须保留财务比率的原始分子分母、公司规模、困境定义、财年、披露时间和证券映射。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Retain raw ratio numerators and denominators, firm size, distress definition, fiscal year, disclosure timing, and security mapping. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"模型说明会计变量可被用于研究困境结果的条件关联，但不把估计概率视为某家公司必然的未来状态。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The model supports conditional association between accounting variables and distress outcomes, not a certain future state for any company. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"以披露时点而非财年末对齐输入，记录重述、合并范围和标签期限，并检查类别不平衡与样本外定义。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Align inputs to disclosure time rather than fiscal year-end; record restatements, consolidation, label horizon, imbalance, and out-of-sample definitions. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Accounting Research (1980)。破产制度、会计准则和公司样本随时间与国家变化；历史概率模型不构成当前信用判断或融资建议。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Accounting Research (1980). Bankruptcy regimes, accounting standards, and firm samples change by time and country; a historical probability model is not current credit advice. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。破产制度、会计准则和公司样本随时间与国家变化；历史概率模型不构成当前信用判断或融资建议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
